{"id":"h274","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Watson and Crick published the double-helix structure of DNA in 1949.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"Watson and Crick proposed the double-helix structure of DNA.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0385},{"text":"The claim names the right scientists and the right molecule.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0171},{"text":"Work leading to the model, including Chargaff's base-composition data, was underway in the late 1940s.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":1.0132},{"text":"Chargaff's data may be the source of the wrong date in the claim.","confidence":0.5,"lean":0.0,"theta":0.7854,"phi":2.1578},{"text":"Watson and Crick published their double-helix model in Nature in April 1953.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":2.9938},{"text":"The claim is false because its date of 1949 is wrong.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":2.945},{"text":"The date is the central factual assertion of the claim.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.0432},{"text":"Preliminary research and related data from 1949 do not amount to publication of the structure.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":2.7679},{"text":"The publication year is what decides the matter.","confidence":0.92,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":3.0432}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":5,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":8,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":5,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relati